<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.12.4: Possible Equation for a Function on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01468</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.12.4: Possible Equation for a Function on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6729ab16-b788-4137-ac3b-733b3dabef62</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Examine the three graphs representing three exponential functions: \(f\), \(g\), and \(h\).</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_14_09_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para>The functions \(f\) and \(h\) are defined as:</para>
      <list>
        <item>\(f(x)=10 \cdot 2^x\)</item>
        <item>\(h(x)=20 \cdot 4^x\)</item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_8349eeef-9ab1-4105-bcd7-065b0c411f0f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following could define function \(g\)? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(g(x)=20 \cdot (1.5)^x\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x)=20 \cdot (2.5)^x\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x)=10 \cdot (3.5)^x\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x)=20 \cdot (4.5)^x\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(g(x)=20 \cdot (2.5)^x\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Explain your reasoning.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>The graph of \(g\) has the same \(y\)-intercept as the graph of \(h\), which is 20. It grows more quickly than \(f\) but more slowly than \(h\),<emphasis effect="italics"> </emphasis>so the growth factor must be greater than 2 but less than 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
